<Layout title="About Baseline" description="Baseline is an independent NBA redraft publication. Learn how our strategy guides, editorial editions, and verified league recaps work." active="about">
  <div class="about-page wrap"><p class="section-label">About the publication</p><h1>Good decisions<br />outlast a hot streak.</h1><div class="about-layout"><p class="about-lead">Baseline is a reading room for fantasy basketball managers. We start with NBA redraft: draft a fresh roster each season, then make it better one decision at a time.</p><div class="article-body"><h2>What you can read today</h2><p>Eight original strategy guides cover league settings, draft choices, weekly planning, and roster moves. They form four editorial guide editions for the 2026–27 season.</p><p>Every starter guide publishes on October 9, 2026. Edition numbers organize the reading sequence. They do not represent NBA game weeks or league results.</p><h2 id="editorial-policy">Our editorial policy</h2><p>The starter guides carry the byline “Baseline Editorial (AI-assisted).” Codex writes these guides with AI assistance. Michael owns the publication; this byline does not claim he writes or verifies each guide.</p><p>Guides present general decision frameworks. They do not claim current player rankings, injury news, schedule counts, or league scores. Public references explain scoring and basketball terms.</p><p>League recaps appear after verified article content is supplied. Recaps must identify their sources, verifier, and verification date. We do not collect private messages or publish invented scores, results, or quotes.</p><h2>A library for the whole season</h2><p>The archive groups articles by season and week. Search by subject or filter by article type. Each edition has a permanent link, and article links keep your archive filters.</p><p><a href="/archive/">Browse the archive</a> or follow the <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a> for new articles.</p><h2>Independent by design</h2><p>Baseline is not affiliated with the NBA or a fantasy platform. NBA names identify the sport we cover. The court illustration is original artwork.</p></div></div></div>
</Layout>
